<main id="top"><section class="hero editorial-wrap snap-section" data-reveal data-section-target="top"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Founder & CEO · OMIX Systems · Kenya</p><h1>I build products,<br/><em>systems</em> and companies.</h1><p class="hero-lede">In that order.</p><p class="hero-intro">I'm Gideon Langat, a software developer and product builder. I lead OMIX Systems, where I turn ideas into digital products and the systems behind them.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button dark magnetic" href="#work">See the work</a><a class="text-link" href="https://omixsystems.store/">Explore OMIX →</a></div></div><figure class="hero-photo depth" data-parallax="0.12"><picture><source media="(max-width: 900px)" srcset={img('gideon-logo.webp')}/><img src={img('gideon-profile.webp')} alt="Gideon Langat" fetchpriority="high"/></picture><figcaption>GIDEON LANGAT · 2026</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="about" class="editorial-wrap section-block snap-section" data-reveal data-section-target="about"><div class="section-label">01 / Hello</div><div class="two-column"><h2>I like building things that connect.</h2><div class="prose"><p>Software is rarely useful in isolation. The product, the data, the people using it and the services underneath all have to make sense together.</p><p>That is the thinking behind my work. I move between engineering, product decisions and the business questions around them — building systems that are practical first and ambitious second.</p><p>OMIX Systems is the company I am building around that philosophy.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="work" class="editorial-wrap section-block snap-section" data-reveal data-section-target="work"><div class="section-label">02 / Selected product work</div><div class="work-list">{work.map(item=><article class="work-item depth" data-parallax="0.06"><div class="work-index">{item.n}</div><div class="work-content"><p class="eyebrow">{item.type}</p><h3>{item.name}</h3><h4>{item.title}</h4><p>{item.body}</p><a class="magnetic" href={item.href}>View project <span>↗</span></a></div></article>)}</div></section>
<section id="current" class="editorial-wrap section-block snap-section" data-reveal data-section-target="current"><div class="section-label">03 / Currently building</div><div class="current-grid"><h2>Not everything needs to be finished to be worth building.</h2><div class="current-copy"><p>Veyra. Phikila. OMIX Marketplace. OMIX Journal. New experiments. Infrastructure that supports them.</p><p>I keep a portfolio because the work changes. This is a record of what is being built now, not a museum of finished projects.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://blog.omixsystems.store/">Read the journal →</a></div></div></section>
<section id="build" class="editorial-wrap section-block snap-section" data-reveal data-section-target="build"><div class="section-label">04 / How I build</div><div class="capability-list">{capabilities.map(([n,title,text])=><div class="capability"><span>{n}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></div>)}</div></section>
<section id="notes" class="editorial-wrap section-block snap-section" data-reveal data-section-target="notes"><div class="section-label">05 / Notes from building OMIX</div><div class="two-column notes-head"><h2>Things I'm thinking about.</h2><p class="prose">Writing is where I slow down enough to explain the decisions behind the products.</p></div><div class="notes-list"><a href="https://blog.omixsystems.store/" class="note-row"><span>Engineering</span><strong>Why modular systems matter</strong><span>↗</span></a><a href="https://blog.omixsystems.store/" class="note-row"><span>Founder notes</span><strong>Building products through OMIX</strong><span>↗</span></a><a href="https://blog.omixsystems.store/" class="note-row"><span>Product</span><strong>What makes software useful?</strong><span>↗</span></a></div></section>
<section id="life" class="editorial-wrap section-block snap-section" data-reveal data-section-target="life"><div class="section-label">06 / Outside the code</div><div class="life-grid"><div class="life-copy"><h2>There's more to building than sitting at a screen.</h2><p>These are the parts of life that do not fit neatly into a CV — time outside, games, experiments, and the people and places that keep the work in perspective.</p></div><div class="life-images"><figure class="depth" data-parallax="0.10"><img src={img('gideon-outdoors.webp')} alt="Gideon outdoors" loading="lazy"/></figure><figure class="depth" data-parallax="0.16"><img src={img('gideon-gaming.webp')} alt="Gideon gaming" loading="lazy"/></figure><figure class="depth wide" data-parallax="0.08"><img src={img('gideon-workspace.webp')} alt="Gideon workspace" loading="lazy"/></figure></div></div></section>
<section id="omix" class="omix-panel snap-section" data-reveal data-section-target="omix"><div class="editorial-wrap"><p class="eyebrow">07 / The company behind the work</p><h2>OMIX Systems</h2><p>Optimal Modular Integration Experts.</p><p class="omix-description">I founded OMIX to build digital products and integrated software systems that solve practical problems.</p><a class="button light magnetic" href="https://omixsystems.store/">Visit OMIX Systems ↗</a></div></section><section id="contact" class="editorial-wrap contact-section section-block snap-section" data-reveal data-section-target="contact"><div class="section-label">08 / Let's build something</div><h2>Have an idea worth making?</h2><p>Tell me what you are trying to build. If it makes sense, we can work out the system behind it.</p><div class="contact-actions"><button class="button gold magnetic" type="button" data-open-schedule>Schedule a meeting</button><a class="button dark magnetic" href="https://omixsystems.store/">Build with OMIX</a><a class="button outline magnetic" href="mailto:hello@omixsystems.store">Email Gideon</a></div></section></main>
<footer class="site-footer editorial-wrap"><div><strong>GIDEON LANGAT</strong><span>Founder & CEO · OMIX Systems</span></div><div><a href="https://omixsystems.store/">OMIX Systems</a><a href="https://blog.omixsystems.store/">Journal</a><a href="https://github.com/oliver4441">GitHub</a></div><small>© 2026 Gideon Langat. Built through OMIX Systems.</small></footer>
<div class="schedule-overlay" id="scheduleOverlay"><div class="schedule-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="scheduleTitle"><button class="schedule-close" type="button" data-schedule-close aria-label="Close scheduling">\u00d7</button><div class="schedule-progress"><i id="scheduleBar"></i></div><p class="schedule-step" id="scheduleStepLabel">Step 1 of 3</p><h3 id="scheduleTitle">What would you like to talk about?</h3><div class="schedule-pane is-active" data-pane="1"><div class="schedule-options" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Meeting topic"><button type="button" class="schedule-option" data-topic="A new product idea"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>A product idea</strong><span>You have something you want to build.</span></span></button><button type="button" class="schedule-option" data-topic="A project with OMIX"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>A project with OMIX</strong><span>Scope, quote or ongoing work.</span></span></button><button type="button" class="schedule-option" data-topic="Partnership"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>Partnership</strong><span>Collaborations and business.</span></span></button><button type="button" class="schedule-option" data-topic="Just a conversation"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><strong>Just a conversation</strong><span>Advice, questions, or saying hi.</span></span></button></div><p class="schedule-error" hidden>Please pick a topic to continue.</p><div class="schedule-nav"><span></span><button class="button dark" type="button" data-next>Continue \u2192</button></div></div><div class="schedule-pane" data-pane="2"><label class="schedule-field">Your name<input id="scheduleName" type="text" name="name" placeholder="Jane Doe" autocomplete="name"/></label><label class="schedule-field">Email address<input id="scheduleEmail" type="email" name="email" placeholder="jane@example.com" autocomplete="email"/></label><p class="schedule-error" hidden>Please add your name and a valid email so I can reach you.</p><div class="schedule-nav"><button class="text-link" type="button" data-back>\u2190 Back</button><button class="button dark" type="button" data-next>Continue \u2192</button></div></div><div class="schedule-pane" data-pane="3"><label class="schedule-field">Anything I should know first? <span style="text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0">(optional)</span><textarea id="scheduleNotes" placeholder="A sentence or two about what you want to discuss\u2026"></textarea></label><div class="schedule-summary" id="scheduleSummary"></div><div class="schedule-nav"><button class="text-link" type="button" data-back>\u2190 Back</button><a class="button gold" id="scheduleGo" href="https://calendly.com/twistedoliver211fs/discussion" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pick a time \u2192</a></div><p class="schedule-note">You will choose a day and time on the next screen \u2014 your details carry over automatically.</p></div><div class="schedule-pane" data-pane="4"><p class="schedule-done-text">My calendar should now be open in a new tab with your details already filled in. Pick a time that suits you \u2014 I look forward to talking.</p><div class="schedule-nav"><a class="text-link" id="scheduleReopen" href="https://calendly.com/twistedoliver211fs/discussion" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reopen calendar</a><button class="button outline" type="button" data-schedule-close>Done</button></div></div></div></div>
<script is:inline>const reduce=matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;const mobile=matchMedia('(max-width: 900px)');const reveal=new IntersectionObserver(e=>e.forEach(x=>{if(x.isIntersecting)x.target.classList.add('is-visible')}),{threshold:mobile.matches?.08:.14,rootMargin:'0px 0px -8% 0px'});document.querySelectorAll('[data-reveal]').forEach(e=>reveal.observe(e));const sections=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-section-target]')],railLinks=[...document.querySelectorAll('.rail-link')],mobileLinks=[...document.querySelectorAll('.mobile-index-links a')],topLinks=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-top-link]')];const setActive=id=>{railLinks.forEach(a=>a.classList.toggle('is-active',a.dataset.section===id));mobileLinks.forEach(a=>a.classList.toggle('is-active',a.dataset.section===id));topLinks.forEach(a=>a.classList.toggle('is-active',a.dataset.topLink===id));const progress=document.querySelector('.rail-progress i');if(progress){progress.style.transform=`scaleY(${Math.max(0,(sections.findIndex(s=>s.dataset.sectionTarget===id)+1)/sections.length)})`}};const sectionObserver=new IntersectionObserver(entries=>entries.forEach(entry=>{if(entry.isIntersecting)setActive(entry.target.dataset.sectionTarget)}),{rootMargin:'-38% 0px -52% 0px',threshold:0});sections.forEach(s=>sectionObserver.observe(s));document.querySelectorAll('.rail-link,.mobile-index-links a,.nav-links a').forEach(a=>a.addEventListener('click',()=>{document.body.classList.remove('index-open');document.querySelector('.mobile-index-toggle')?.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false')}));const toggle=document.querySelector('.mobile-index-toggle'),close=document.querySelector('[data-close-index]');toggle?.addEventListener('click',()=>{const open=!document.body.classList.contains('index-open');document.body.classList.toggle('index-open',open);toggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded',String(open))});close?.addEventListener('click',()=>{document.body.classList.remove('index-open');toggle?.setAttribute('ari